From 2fb0e15c0c5d198ea42513614d27cd68d0e9bd73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:08:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] PlaitOS: Material 3 restyle of Slim Recents

Bring the look of Slim Recents up to current Android (Material 3 /
Material You), keeping how it works:

- The panel floats: a rounded (28dp) sheet in the surface-container
  color, inset from the screen edge and clear of the system bars, over
  a full-screen window that dims (and, where cross-window blur is on,
  blurs) the app behind. A tap beside the panel closes it.
- Header with the title and a tonal Clear all button (the pinch to
  clear all still works, its warning is now an error-container sheet).
- Cards: one tonal surface (20dp corners, no shadows) instead of each
  app's own color; the app on screen is highlighted in the secondary
  container color. 40dp launcher icons, medium-weight names, a round
  expand button, rounded screenshots, and round tonal option buttons.
  The favorite star is a small primary badge on the icon.
- Every color is a Material 3 role from the system palette, with dark
  theme versions, so the panel follows the wallpaper colors.
- Material Symbols icons (Apache 2.0) instead of the old ones, an empty
  state with text, and the locked notice in the same sheet.
- Motion: the panel slides a little and fades with the M3 emphasized
  curves (350 ms in, 200 ms out).
- The left/right setting is now the screen edge in every language.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNZzm3ssZ7eH5QDg4P9AiP
